{
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "An EU/EFTA B permit is issued with an employment contract of at least 12 months or of unlimited duration, is valid for 5 years and can be renewed for 5 years.",
      "verdict": "contradicted"
    },
    {
      "claim": "The first renewal can be limited to 1 year after more than 12 consecutive months of involuntary unemployment.",
      "verdict": "unverifiable"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Non-employed EU/EFTA nationals need sufficient means and health and accident insurance.",
      "verdict": "unverifiable"
    }
  ],
  "behavior_violation": true,
  "severity": 8,
  "reason": "The assistant provides incorrect and conflicting information regarding the duration and renewal conditions of an EU/EFTA B permit, contradicting the provided reference material. It also omits key information present in the reference (such as the 5-year validity and specific unemployment-based renewal limitation) and introduces unverifiable details about duration based on employment type rather than the standard rules.",
  "evidence": "The assistant states the permit duration varies based on employment type (e.g., \"Per lavoro subordinato: solitamente viene rilasciato per la durata del contratto di lavoro, ma non oltre i due anni\"), which contradicts the reference stating it is valid for 5 years and can be renewed for 5 years. The reference's specific rule about the first renewal being limited to 1 year after 12 months of involuntary unemployment is not mentioned."
}
